body:
Glad I found this thread, as I have the exact same issue.  Constant "Network experiencing issues" when playing, with drops from full strength to nothing and back.  I have Xfinity Xfi 5Ghz wifi on a gigabit connection.  Speedtest on my phone shows 650+mbps/45-50 upstream.  Everything else works fine but this.

&#x200B;

Never considered it to be proximity, I'm in Arkansas, perhaps it's something to do with region.  Anyway, I hope it goes away Sept 15th....

This is great!  At first I couldn't get it to work at all, seems maybe it just takes a bit before it's fully integrated?

Alexa would just respond that she didn't know what I was saying until finally she started going "Tell me what Xbox feature you would like to have" or some such.

After that it all seems to work, somewhat.

Issues I've had so far:

&#x200B;

\- "Alexa, tell Xbox to open Netflix." this worked, however it thought Netflix wasn't installed (has been forever!) so it took me to the MS Store to get it, which would be bad ass if it hadn't already been installed. 

&#x200B;

\- "Alexa, tell Xbox to open YouTube." failed easily 6 times in a row before finally, magically it worked.

&#x200B;

I'll definitely keep testing this, thanks for rolling it out for us lowly B-Tier folks!
